 "notes": "E6 test case dataset. Two state tenants of 500 field workers, eight NGO tenants sharing 500, at day 365. The fourth growth point, added because case 8's curve is the only evidence the exercise produces about scale beyond the pilot, and three points over 180 days is a short baseline. Rolling data means year two accrues at year one's rate, so volume keeps climbing. bundle_path and bundle_revision must be filled in before generating. A tenant may also carry its own bundle_path, which is how H1's 'cover the range of organisation size' is done -- config size drives the syncDetails row count organisation_id is null on every tenant and must be filled in before generating. It held 1-10, which are not free: on the load environment 1 is the platform organisation, 3 the customer's, 9 a fixture and 10 the first state tenant. Those ids were placeholders from before any tenant was provisioned, and generating against them would have written a pilot dataset into four live organisations. Provision the ten tenants, dump refs.json, and record the ids the server assigned.",
